Acceptance criteria:
- Default lighting reads warmer and softer than the rejected harsh spotlight;
  actual captures are reviewed, without claiming subjective user acceptance.
- Room lights toggle independently of lamp, LCD, pause and console power.
- Switching off both room and lamp retains LCD-only lighting and real power off.
- The larger power cap is genuinely visible from play view and its touch target
  fits desktop/phone viewports, stays off the LCD and operates real power state.
- Existing saves, native settings, mapped input, inspection and cartridge behavior remain.
- Larger LCD preserves 3:2 mapping; top/bottom/side bezel gaps are approximately
  half their previous dimensions, with retained curved/rectangular shader switching.

